  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nSurface high pressure builds in across the Ohio Valley from the \nnorthwest through Friday. Dry conditions and below average \ntemperatures persist with lows in the 50s and highs in the 70s to \nnear 80. \n\nThe surface high shifts east this weekend which will allow warmer \ntemperatures and higher dew points to move back into the area from \nthe south. Shower and thunderstorms chances return with heat and\nmoisture. Upper level shortwave troughs moving through the \nnorthwesterly flow aloft could lead to periods of greater storm \ncoverage at times.",
